The existing module takes a better route than the rejected planted-maximal-clique idea: it uses the paper’s exact clique-probability identity as a Track B telescoping problem. I found two audit issues to fix before rerunning anything: the checker must validate that the supplied index programs are genuinely bijections, and the canonical key currently mishandles lane relabellings when lane lengths differ. I’m patching those, plus making the declared sampling language exact.
