89:\subsection{Enumerating Only Large Maximal Cliques}
96:Algorithm~\ref{algo:largemule} runs on the pruned uncertain graph $\ugraph'$ to enumerate only large maximal cliques. The recursive method in Algorithm~\ref{algo:large} differs from Algorithm~\ref{algo:dfs} as follows. Before each recursive call to method Enum-Uncertain-MC-Large (Algorithm~\ref{algo:large}), the algorithm checks if the sum of the sizes of the current working clique $C'$ and the candidate vertex set $I'$ are greater than the size threshold $t$. If not, the recursive method is not called. This optimization leads to a substantial pruning of the search space and hence a reduction in runtime.
