codex
No generator is shipped: the paper has no family that clears G, H, V, and the answer-size requirements simultaneously.

- Finding one α-maximal clique is polynomial via greedy extension using the paper’s Observation 2.
- Enumerating all α-maximal cliques can require exponentially many output atoms by Theorem 1.
- The native Track B probability construction passed every local gate, but the bare oracle solved every completed attempt: 11/11 across four levels.
- Its reference route averaged 5,171,460 operations and 1.88 seconds, versus a 19-operation compact route—so the shortcut was simply too visible.

The decision and supporting measurements are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1310.6780/REJECTED.md). The experimental module is retained as [rejected_gen_1310_6780.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1310.6780/rejected_gen_1310_6780.py), with its [self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1310.6780/simple_selftest_report.json) and [oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1310.6780/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl).

The rejection is grounded in the full [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.6780), particularly Sections 2–4 and Theorems 1–3.
